{"id":"chatcmpl-6c41252d-279a-4a6e-8c53-20504a0b5f3b","object":"chat.completion","created":1795247979,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a visual comparison strategy for laterality-dependent medical image findings: use orientation markers to establish patient left/right, then compare relative positions of paired structures. The solution cross-validates a primary expert tool's claim with an independent grounded report before committing to an answer. The key abstraction is 'establish frame of reference first, then compare, then corroborate.'\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question asks which of two sides/structures is affected, first establish the patient's orientation frame (e.g., laterality markers) before comparing relative positions.\",\n    \"For paired-structure comparison tasks, query a domain expert tool with an explicit comparison instruction rather than an open-ended 'what do you see' prompt.\",\n    \"Corroborate a single-tool finding with an independent second source (grounded report or visual inspection) before finalizing the answer.\",\n    \"When options are mutually exclusive binary pairs (left vs right, elevated vs normal), structure reasoning as a direct A-vs-B comparison to avoid ambiguity.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always resolve orientation/laterality markers first; compare paired anatomy (hemidiaphragms, lungs, kidneys) by relative height/position; confirm with a second independent read.\",\n    \"Binary visual comparison tasks\": \"Frame the question as an explicit comparison between the two candidate options; use a tool prompt that names both candidates to force a discriminating judgment.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted QA with expert models\": \"Use a specialized expert tool for the primary claim, then cross-check with a general grounded-report tool; reconcile before answering.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation/laterality marker (e.g., 'L') is identified before interpreting left vs right.\",\n    \"Verify the primary tool's finding is consistent with an independent second source or direct visual inspection.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":452,"total_tokens":846,"completion_tokens":394,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":452},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":394}}}